---
// (7) Night owls, sunset to sunrise, with moon phases. Chart: src/scripts/sections/owls.js
import PhotoCredit from '../PhotoCredit.astro';
import SectionNumber from '../SectionNumber.astro';
import { sectionTitle } from '../../site.config.js';
const id = 'owls-sec';
---
<section class="panel owls" id={id} aria-labelledby="h-owls">
  <canvas class="art cut" id="cv-owls" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="gutter" style="position:relative">
    <SectionNumber id={id} />
    <h2 id="h-owls" class="ink">{sectionTitle(id)}</h2>
    <p class="prose ink">Two species of owl, with fourteen calls. Tawny owls were heard on four nights, the first on 15 August. Barn owls were heard in September, on three nights, and were almost always detected with high confidence: five of six calls at 100%. Both the tawny owl and barn owl were detected on the night of 21–22 September.</p>
    <p class="prose ink">The small moons on the y-axis show the moon's phase on that night. Most owl nights were dark ones: on four of the six nights, the moon was about a third lit or less.</p>
    <div class="night-wrap"><div class="night" id="night"></div></div>
    <ul class="owl-key ink"><li><i style="background:#F2B06A"></i>Tawny Owl</li><li><i style="background:#EFE9DE"></i>Barn Owl</li></ul>
  </div>
  <PhotoCredit name="Branimir Balogović" />
</section>
